# RUN: %stinkytofu-opt --arch gfx1250 %s --LiftAsmRegistersToSSAPass --DumpStinkyModulePass=ssaForm,stdout
#
# LiftAsmRegistersToSSAPass: unsupported input leaves the function untouched.
#
# Accumulator registers are not lifted yet: on some architectures an AGPR and a
# VGPR name the same storage, and building two SSA values over one physical
# register would be unsound. So nothing is attached to this function.
#
# That is the fallback contract: lifting reports a missed optimization rather
# than failing the compilation, and a function with no attached SSA is a valid
# pre-lift function. The physical instruction stream must survive unchanged so
# the legacy path still works, which is also why an ssaForm dump of an unlifted
# function is just the physical program.
#
# CHECK-LABEL: st.func @lift_asm_registers_to_ssa_unsupported
#
# No block arguments, because nothing was lifted.
# CHECK-NEXT: ^entry:
#
# The physical program is intact, accumulator operand included.
# CHECK-NEXT: a[10:17] = "st.v_wmma_f32_16x16x32_bf16"(v[20:27], v[30:37], a[10:17])
# CHECK-NEXT: v3 = "st.v_add_f32"(v2, v1)
#
# Nothing partial was attached: no SSA value names appear at all.
# CHECK-NOT: %

st.func @lift_asm_registers_to_ssa_unsupported() {
^entry:
  a[10:17] = "st.v_wmma_f32_16x16x32_bf16"(v[20:27], v[30:37], a[10:17])
  v3 = "st.v_add_f32"(v2, v1)
}
